WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:01.870
- You know what I need?

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:05.038
A cool nickname, like CNC Music Factory.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.533
No, that's not cool.

00:00:07.452 --> 00:00:10.600
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez has
been a member of Congress

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.920
for less than a month.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.670
At this time last year, no
one outside of New York City,

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.790
and even lots of people
inside New York City,

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.490
had literally never heard of her.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:25.200
Which is what makes this
fact all the more incredible.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.010
In a late January CNN poll,
almost six in 10 Americans

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.870
not only know her name, but
also have an opinion about her.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.550
That opinion is, slightly, negative.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.480
27% of people have a favorable view

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.430
of the new New York congresswoman,

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:43.200
while 32% have a negative view.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.568
But that's not the real story.

00:00:45.568 --> 00:00:49.610
The real story is that a 29
year old first-time candidate,

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.438
who was running as a Democratic Socialist

00:00:51.438 --> 00:00:55.310
against the man many saw as a
future Speaker of the House,

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:58.970
has rapidly become one
of the most recognizable

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:02.330
faces in the Democratic Party nationally.

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.260
Now think about these numbers.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.582
41% of people say they either
have never heard of AOC

00:01:07.582 --> 00:01:11.000
or don't know enough about
her to have an opinion.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.860
In that same CNN poll, 28% of people said

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:17.020
they either hadn't
heard of Mitch McConnell

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.574
or didn't know enough about
him to offer an opinion.

00:01:19.574 --> 00:01:23.120
Mitch McConnell is the freaking
Senate Majority Leader.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.290
He has been in the Senate since 1984.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:32.040
If you turn on cable TV for an
hour on any day of the week.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.670
You should do that, by the way.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:35.302
You have a decent chance of either seeing

00:01:35.302 --> 00:01:38.129
or hearing or both McConnell.

00:01:38.129 --> 00:01:40.245
And yet, Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez

00:01:40.245 --> 00:01:42.350
is within shouting distance

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:46.810
of McConnell when it comes
to how many people know her.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.670
Or, look at this in another way.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:51.890
Stacey Abrams was one of
the shining Democratic stars

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:53.220
of the 2018 election,

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.680
running to be the first African American

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.560
female governor in the country.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.520
Abrams came within a hairsbreadth

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.077
of winning in the
reddish state of Georgia.

00:02:02.077 --> 00:02:04.730
So popular was Abrams
among the Democratic base,

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:07.300
that congressional Democrats asked her

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.370
to deliver the Democratic response

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:12.100
to Trump's State of the Union Address.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.550
Given Abram's high profile,

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.710
she must be nearly as well-known

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:18.990
as Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, right?

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:19.823
Wrong!
(buzzer dings)

00:02:19.823 --> 00:02:21.933
Sorry, that was a little harsh.

00:02:21.933 --> 00:02:25.110
Six in 10 people in the CNN
poll had never heard of Abrams.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:29.010
Or didn't know enough to
offer an opinion about her.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:33.250
So, how the heck did
AOC get to this point,

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:36.960
and more importantly,
what will she do now?

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.160
Alright, the first question
is easier to answer,

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:40.850
so I'm gonna try and
answer that one first.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:43.360
Ocasio-Cortez's win over then-congressman,

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.260
Joe Crowley, was national news,

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.170
and her stunned reaction
to her victory went viral,

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:52.752
which, had it ended there,
would have made a nice story.

00:02:52.752 --> 00:02:55.276
But it would not have
turned a freshman member

00:02:55.276 --> 00:02:58.101
from a safely Democratic seat in a

00:02:58.101 --> 00:03:02.820
largely Democratic state
into a national superstar.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.380
Of course, it didn't end there.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.988
Ocasio-Cortez's victory
became, for liberals,

00:03:07.988 --> 00:03:09.860
a rallying point.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:13.190
A tangible sign that voters
in the Democratic base

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.430
weren't just fed up with Republicans,

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:18.730
but also were sick of
lots of their own members

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:21.334
and their own party establishment too.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.920
Crowley was a symbol of the status quo

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.100
and compromise driven politics.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:31.100
AOC was new blood, using
confrontation as political strategy

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:34.028
and saying exactly what she thought,

00:03:34.028 --> 00:03:37.840
no matter the supposed
political consequences.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.421
Now, even as AOC was becoming
a hero to the liberalist left,

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:45.430
she was becoming a villain

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.730
to conservatives around the country.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:48.563
Sidebar!

00:03:48.563 --> 00:03:51.477
Which came first: the liberal
love or the conservative hate?

00:03:51.477 --> 00:03:53.310
Chicken and the egg, my dude.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:57.010
For conservatives, Ocasio-Cortez's
unapologetic embrace

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.230
of democratic socialism,

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:00.908
her support for hugely high
tax rates on the very wealthy,

00:04:00.908 --> 00:04:04.650
and her backing of medicare for all,

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.351
made her the poster child for what

00:04:06.351 --> 00:04:11.110
they believe the disastrous
future Democrats want.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:13.009
Now, that Ocasio-Cortez was,

00:04:13.009 --> 00:04:16.200
and is, in her 20s, is a Latina,

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.620
and maintains a hugely active social media

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:22.480
presence all served to
further fuel the fires

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:24.438
on the left and the right about her.

00:04:24.438 --> 00:04:26.530
And yet, here we are.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:30.880
A 29 year old freshman member
of Congress known by 60%

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:33.400
of the total population with very strong

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.531
views held about her on both
sides of the political aisle.

00:04:36.531 --> 00:04:38.730
Okay, so now for the tougher question.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:41.244
What does AOC do next?

00:04:41.244 --> 00:04:43.170
It's actually easier to answer what

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.330
she probably won't do next.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:48.630
She's very, very unlikely
to moderate her views

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.370
or worry too much about the fact that

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:53.600
she has become the latest
Republican boogeywoman.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.100
She's also not going to
play the traditional role

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.993
of a newly elected member of Congress.

00:04:57.993 --> 00:05:01.330
Sort of sit and watch while
the more experienced members,

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.000
you know, handle things.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.920
After Ocasio-Cortez's election,

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.665
and even before she
took the oath of office,

00:05:07.665 --> 00:05:12.000
she participated in a sit in
at Nancy Pelosi's office aimed

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.890
at convincing the Speaker to
take action on climate change.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:18.180
Not exactly shining and retiring move.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:21.030
Ocasio-Cortez has also
drawn considerable attention

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:23.858
for her promotion of what
she calls a Green New Deal,

00:05:23.858 --> 00:05:27.647
which she is promised will
be quote, "national, social,

00:05:27.647 --> 00:05:30.687
"industrial and economic mobilization at a

00:05:30.687 --> 00:05:34.290
"scale not seen since
World War II," end quote.

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:35.980
Now she's expected to introduce that

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.440
legislation in the House in mid-February.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.303
Already some Democrats are talking about

00:05:41.303 --> 00:05:45.140
Ocasio-Cortez as a potential
presidential candidate.

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:46.530
There's just one problem with that,

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:50.500
she won't be eligible to run
for that for another six years.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:51.870
You have to be 35.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.090
Now predicting what will happen

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:57.658
six years in the future is a
fool's errand and I am no fool.

00:05:57.658 --> 00:06:00.180
At least not today.

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.710
And that is the point.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.560
We do this every week twice.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:07.853
Check back every Tuesday and
Thursday for new episodes.

